#: optiondialog.cpp:194
msgid "Chooses the type of bitmap fonts used for the display. As a general rule, the higher the dpi value, the better quality of the output. On the other hand, large dpi fonts use more resources and make KDVI slower. \nIf you are low on hard disk space, or have a slow machine, you may want to choose the same setting that is also used by dvips. That way you avoid to generate several bitmap versions of the same font."
msgstr ""

